---
title: Models built forward, for the measure theorist
summary: Why an abstract probability space serves modelling as an abstract vector space serves linear algebra, why the way back to coordinates is harder in probability, and how building a model forward from densities restores it, so that every random variable factors through the quantities and every expectation is an explicit integral.
---

